<p>The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) rose 5 points but is still net negative at -9. This indicator hasn’t been positive in more than four years.</p>
<p>Inflation expectations lifted slightly from 5.1% to 5.2%.</p>
</div><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-separator_207570709__1346191401"><hr class="block h-6 p-0 m-0 border-none separator" cqType="anzconz/components/separator" cqPath="/content/anzconz/nz/en/about-us/economic-markets-research/consumer-confidence/jcr:content/root/responsivegrid/tabs_copy_copy/item_1738272454047/columncontainer/responsivegrid/responsivegrid/separator_207570709__1346191401" componentProperties="[object Object]"/><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-standalonecta_156915_1988683461"><div class="standalone-cta relative"><a class="link underline semantic-text-accent1 link--no-underline btn button-icon--download inline-flex items-center btn--theme-light btn--variation-tertiary" href="/content/dam/anzconz/documents/economics-and-market-research/2025/ANZ-ConsumerConfidence-20251128.pdf" target="_self" download="">ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence, November 2025: Looking up?<span class="link-text">(PDF 622.5KB)</span><i aria-hidden="true" class="Icon inline-block align-middle leading-none font-normal not-italic no-underline normal-case antialiased text-ico-16 w-4 h-4 Icon--download" style="font-family:iconfont;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:1;text-rendering:optimizeLegibility;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;-moz-osx-font-smoothing:grayscale;font-size:16px;width:16px;height:16px"></i></a></div><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-separator_207570709_"><hr class="block h-6 p-0 m-0 border-none separator" cqType="anzconz/components/separator" cqPath="/content/anzconz/nz/en/about-us/economic-markets-research/consumer-confidence/jcr:content/root/responsivegrid/tabs_copy_copy/item_1738272454047/columncontainer/responsivegrid/responsivegrid/separator_207570709_" componentProperties="[object Object]"/><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-title_1164321089_cop_1143728336"><h3 class="text-h3-xs lg:text-h3-lg xl:text-h3-xl font-semibold mb-4 lg:mb-5 semantic-text-heading" id="title_988872689"><div class="rt-content" data-rte-editelement="true">October&nbsp;2025</div></h3><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-text_803677586"><div class="rt-content" id="_content_anzconz_nz_en_about-us_economic-markets-research_consumer-confidence_jcr_content_root_responsivegrid_tabs_copy_copy_item_1738272454047_columncontainer_responsivegrid_responsivegrid_text_803677586" data-rte-editelement="true"><p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence fell slightly from 94.6 to 92.4 in October, giving up last month’s gains.</p>
<p>The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) fell from -11 to -14. This indicator hasn’t been positive in more than four years.</p>
<p>Inflation expectations lifted from 4.8% to 5.1%.</p>
</div><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-separator_207570709__2118938729"><hr class="block h-6 p-0 m-0 border-none separator" cqType="anzconz/components/separator" cqPath="/content/anzconz/nz/en/about-us/economic-markets-research/consumer-confidence/jcr:content/root/responsivegrid/tabs_copy_copy/item_1738272454047/columncontainer/responsivegrid/responsivegrid/separator_207570709__2118938729" componentProperties="[object Object]"/><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-standalonecta_156915_1647778701"><div class="standalone-cta relative"><a class="link underline semantic-text-accent1 link--no-underline btn button-icon--download inline-flex items-center btn--theme-light btn--variation-tertiary" href="/content/dam/anzconz/documents/economics-and-market-research/2025/ANZ-ConsumerConfidence-20251031.pdf" target="_self" download="">ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence, October 2025: Stalled<span class="link-text">(PDF 623KB)</span><i aria-hidden="true" class="Icon inline-block align-middle leading-none font-normal not-italic no-underline normal-case antialiased text-ico-16 w-4 h-4 Icon--download" style="font-family:iconfont;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:1;text-rendering:optimizeLegibility;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;-moz-osx-font-smoothing:grayscale;font-size:16px;width:16px;height:16px"></i></a></div><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-separator_207570709"><hr class="block h-6 p-0 m-0 border-none separator" cqType="anzconz/components/separator" cqPath="/content/anzconz/nz/en/about-us/economic-markets-research/consumer-confidence/jcr:content/root/responsivegrid/tabs_copy_copy/item_1738272454047/columncontainer/responsivegrid/responsivegrid/separator_207570709" componentProperties="[object Object]"/><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-title_1164321089_cop_1077296375"><h3 class="text-h3-xs lg:text-h3-lg xl:text-h3-xl font-semibold mb-4 lg:mb-5 semantic-text-heading" id="title_870352344"><div class="rt-content" data-rte-editelement="true">September 2025</div></h3><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-text_1848906934_copy_365528341"><div class="rt-content" id="_content_anzconz_nz_en_about-us_economic-markets-research_consumer-confidence_jcr_content_root_responsivegrid_tabs_copy_copy_item_1738272454047_columncontainer_responsivegrid_responsivegrid_text_1848906934_copy_365528341" data-rte-editelement="true"><p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence rose from 92.0 to 94.6 in September, unwinding the fall seen last month. Confidence was markedly lower in the days following the release of the very weak Q2 GDP data. The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) rose 1 point to -11. Inflation expectations were steady at 4.8%.</p>
</div><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-separator_207570709__430474675"><hr class="block h-6 p-0 m-0 border-none separator" cqType="anzconz/components/separator" cqPath="/content/anzconz/nz/en/about-us/economic-markets-research/consumer-confidence/jcr:content/root/responsivegrid/tabs_copy_copy/item_1738272454047/columncontainer/responsivegrid/responsivegrid/separator_207570709__430474675" componentProperties="[object Object]"/><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-standalonecta_156915_2106613055"><div class="standalone-cta relative"><a class="link underline semantic-text-accent1 link--no-underline btn button-icon--download inline-flex items-center btn--theme-light btn--variation-tertiary" href="/content/dam/anzconz/documents/economics-and-market-research/2025/ANZ-ConsumerConfidence-20250926.pdf" target="_self" download="">ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence, September 2025: Small lift<span class="link-text">(PDF 600.6KB)</span><i aria-hidden="true" class="Icon inline-block align-middle leading-none font-normal not-italic no-underline normal-case antialiased text-ico-16 w-4 h-4 Icon--download" style="font-family:iconfont;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:1;text-rendering:optimizeLegibility;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;-moz-osx-font-smoothing:grayscale;font-size:16px;width:16px;height:16px"></i></a></div><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-separator_1140789123_1361106557"><hr class="block h-6 p-0 m-0 border-none separator" cqType="anzconz/components/separator" cqPath="/content/anzconz/nz/en/about-us/economic-markets-research/consumer-confidence/jcr:content/root/responsivegrid/tabs_copy_copy/item_1738272454047/columncontainer/responsivegrid/responsivegrid/separator_1140789123_1361106557" componentProperties="[object Object]"/><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-title_1164321089_cop"><h3 class="text-h3-xs lg:text-h3-lg xl:text-h3-xl font-semibold mb-4 lg:mb-5 semantic-text-heading" id="title_294828166"><div class="rt-content" data-rte-editelement="true">August 2025</div></h3><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-text_1848906934_copy"><div class="rt-content" id="_content_anzconz_nz_en_about-us_economic-markets-research_consumer-confidence_jcr_content_root_responsivegrid_tabs_copy_copy_item_1738272454047_columncontainer_responsivegrid_responsivegrid_text_1848906934_copy" data-rte-editelement="true"><p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence fell 3 points to 92 in August, its lowest level in 10 months. The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) fell 4 points to -12. Inflation expectations fell 0.3pts to 4.8%.&nbsp;</p>
