_1140789123_1458488318"><hr class="block h-6 p-0 m-0 border-none separator" cqType="anzconz/components/separator" cqPath="/content/anzconz/nz/en/about-us/economic-markets-research/consumer-confidence/jcr:content/root/responsivegrid/tabs_copy_copy/item_1738272454047/columncontainer/responsivegrid/responsivegrid/separator_1140789123_1458488318" componentProperties="[object Object]"/><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-title_1164321089"><h3 class="text-h3-xs lg:text-h3-lg xl:text-h3-xl font-semibold mb-4 lg:mb-5 semantic-text-heading" id="title_611043135"><div class="rt-content" data-rte-editelement="true">July 2025</div></h3><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-text_1848906934"><div class="rt-content" id="_content_anzconz_nz_en_about-us_economic-markets-research_consumer-confidence_jcr_content_root_responsivegrid_tabs_copy_copy_item_1738272454047_columncontainer_responsivegrid_responsivegrid_text_1848906934" data-rte-editelement="true"><p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence fell 4 points to 94.7 in July, continuing its recent zig-zag pattern. The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) fell 1 point to -8, remaining very weak. Inflation expectations lifted 0.2pts to 5.1%, the highest since April 2023. Food price inflation of 4.2% y/y probably has a lot to do with it.&nbsp;</p>
</div><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-separator_207570709__1841576495"><hr class="block h-6 p-0 m-0 border-none separator" cqType="anzconz/components/separator" cqPath="/content/anzconz/nz/en/about-us/economic-markets-research/consumer-confidence/jcr:content/root/responsivegrid/tabs_copy_copy/item_1738272454047/columncontainer/responsivegrid/responsivegrid/separator_207570709__1841576495" componentProperties="[object Object]"/><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-standalonecta_1569151483"><div class="standalone-cta relative"><a class="link underline semantic-text-accent1 link--no-underline btn button-icon--download inline-flex items-center btn--theme-light btn--variation-tertiary" href="/content/dam/anzconz/documents/economics-and-market-research/2025/ANZ-ConsumerConfidence-20250801.pdf" target="_self" download="">ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence, July 2025: Household inflation expectations crack 5%<span class="link-text">(PDF 635.5KB)</span><i aria-hidden="true" class="Icon inline-block align-middle leading-none font-normal not-italic no-underline normal-case antialiased text-ico-16 w-4 h-4 Icon--download" style="font-family:iconfont;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:1;text-rendering:optimizeLegibility;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;-moz-osx-font-smoothing:grayscale;font-size:16px;width:16px;height:16px"></i></a></div><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-separator_1140789123"><hr class="block h-6 p-0 m-0 border-none separator" cqType="anzconz/components/separator" cqPath="/content/anzconz/nz/en/about-us/economic-markets-research/consumer-confidence/jcr:content/root/responsivegrid/tabs_copy_copy/item_1738272454047/columncontainer/responsivegrid/responsivegrid/separator_1140789123" componentProperties="[object Object]"/><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-title_944583508"><h3 class="text-h3-xs lg:text-h3-lg xl:text-h3-xl font-semibold mb-4 lg:mb-5 semantic-text-heading" id="title_601592832"><div class="rt-content" data-rte-editelement="true">June 2025</div></h3><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-text_492601635"><div class="rt-content" id="_content_anzconz_nz_en_about-us_economic-markets-research_consumer-confidence_jcr_content_root_responsivegrid_tabs_copy_copy_item_1738272454047_columncontainer_responsivegrid_responsivegrid_text_492601635" data-rte-editelement="true"><p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence lifted 6 points to 98.8 in June, a welcome bounce after a fall last month.&nbsp;The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) lifted 3 points, but at -7 it’s very soft. Inflation expectations lifted 0.3pts to 4.9%, the highest since April 2023. That’s probably got quite a lot to do with food price inflation, which is running at 4.4%.</p>
</div><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-separator_207570709__576329774"><hr class="block h-6 p-0 m-0 border-none separator" cqType="anzconz/components/separator" cqPath="/content/anzconz/nz/en/about-us/economic-markets-research/consumer-confidence/jcr:content/root/responsivegrid/tabs_copy_copy/item_1738272454047/columncontainer/responsivegrid/responsivegrid/separator_207570709__576329774" componentProperties="[object Object]"/><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-standalonecta_1966321415"><div class="standalone-cta relative"><a class="link underline semantic-text-accent1 link--no-underline btn button-icon--download inline-flex items-center btn--theme-light btn--variation-tertiary" href="/content/dam/anzconz/documents/economics-and-market-research/2025/ANZ-ConsumerConfidence-20250627.pdf" target="_self" download="">ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence, June 2025: A wintry sunrise<span class="link-text">(PDF 693.3KB)</span><i aria-hidden="true" class="Icon inline-block align-middle leading-none font-normal not-italic no-underline normal-case antialiased text-ico-16 w-4 h-4 Icon--download" style="font-family:iconfont;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:1;text-rendering:optimizeLegibility;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;-moz-osx-font-smoothing:grayscale;font-size:16px;width:16px;height:16px"></i></a></div><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-separator_1901606163"><hr class="block h-6 p-0 m-0 border-none separator" cqType="anzconz/components/separator" cqPath="/content/anzconz/nz/en/about-us/economic-markets-research/consumer-confidence/jcr:content/root/responsivegrid/tabs_copy_copy/item_1738272454047/columncontainer/responsivegrid/responsivegrid/separator_1901606163" componentProperties="[object Object]"/><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-title"><h3 class="text-h3-xs lg:text-h3-lg xl:text-h3-xl font-semibold mb-4 lg:mb-5 semantic-text-heading" id="title_1775033145"><div class="rt-content" data-rte-editelement="true">May 2025</div></h3><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-text"><div class="rt-content" id="_content_anzconz_nz_en_about-us_economic-markets-research_consumer-confidence_jcr_content_root_responsivegrid_tabs_copy_copy_item_1738272454047_columncontainer_responsivegrid_responsivegrid_text" data-rte-editelement="true"><p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence fell 5 points to 92.9 in May, giving up the lift seen in April.&nbsp; The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) lifted 1 point, but at -10 it’s still weak. Inflation expectations eased 0.1pts to 4.6%. That’s a lot higher than a couple of months ago, with the jump possibly caused by global tariff talk.&nbsp;</p>
</div><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-separator_207570709__1322688750"><hr class="block h-6 p-0 m-0 border-none separator" cqType="anzconz/components/separator" cqPath="/content/anzconz/nz/en/about-us/economic-markets-research/consumer-confidence/jcr:content/root/responsivegrid/tabs_copy_copy/item_1738272454047/columncontainer/responsivegrid/responsivegrid/separator_207570709__1322688750" componentProperties="[object Object]"/><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-standalonecta"><div class="standalone-cta relative"><a class="link underline semantic-text-accent1 link--no-underline btn button-icon--download inline-flex items-center btn--theme-light btn--variation-tertiary" href="/content/dam/anzconz/documents/economics-and-market-research/2025/ANZ-ConsumerConfidence-20250530.pdf" target="_self" download="">ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence, May 2025: I&#x27;m blue<span class="link-text">(PDF 681.8KB)</span><i aria-hidden="true" class="Icon inline-block align-middle leading-none font-normal not-italic no-underline normal-case antialiased text-ico-16 w-4 h-4 Icon--download" style="font-family:iconfont;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:1;text-rendering:optimizeLegibility;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;-moz-osx-font-smoothing:grayscale;font-size:16px;width:16px;height:16px"></i></a></div><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-separator_289455847"><hr class="block h-6 p-0 m-0 border-none separator" cqType="anzconz/components/separator" cqPath="/content/anzconz/nz/en/about-us/economic-markets-research/consumer-confidence/jcr:content/root/responsivegrid/tabs_copy_copy/item_1738272454047/columncontainer/responsivegrid/responsivegrid/separator_289455847" componentProperties="[object Object]"/><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-title_66608087_copy__1851913580"><h3 class="text-h3-xs lg:text-h3-lg xl:text-h3-xl font-semibold mb-4 lg:mb-5 semantic-text-heading" id="title_625420846"><div class="rt-content" data-rte-editelement="true">April 2025</div></h3><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-text_2064119929_copy_250696936"><div class="rt-content" id="_content_anzconz_nz_en_about-us_economic-markets-research_consumer-confidence_jcr_content_root_responsivegrid_tabs_copy_copy_item_1738272454047_columncontainer_responsivegrid_responsivegrid_text_2064119929_copy_250696936" data-rte-editelement="true"><p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence rose 5 points to 98.3 in April, shoring up the upward trend that was starting to look wobbly.&nbsp; The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) rose 5 points, but at -11 it’s still nothing flash. Inflation expectations soared 0.5pts to 4.7%, the highest reading since July 2023. It may be related to global tariff talk, but since New Zealand is not putting on new tariffs, global developments are unlikely to be inflationary here.</p>
</div><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-separator_207570709__160094283"><hr class="block h-6 p-0 m-0 border-none separator" cqType="anzconz/components/separator" cqPath="/content/anzconz/nz/en/about-us/economic-markets-research/consumer-confidence/jcr:content/root/responsivegrid/tabs_copy_copy/item_1738272454047/columncontainer/responsivegrid/responsivegrid/separator_207570709__160094283" componentProperties="[object Object]"/><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-standalonecta_166377_754981211"><div class="standalone-cta relative"><a class="link underline semantic-text-accent1 link--no-underline btn button-icon--download inline-flex items-center btn--theme-light btn--variation-tertiary" href="/content/dam/anzconz/documents/economics-and-market-research/2025/ANZ-ConsumerConfidence-20250424.pdf" target="_self" download="">ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence, April 2025: Back on the up<span class="link-text">(PDF 671.7KB)</span><i aria-hidden="true" class="Icon inline-block align-middle leading-none font-normal not-italic no-underline normal-case antialiased text-ico-16 w-4 h-4 Icon--download" style="font-family:iconfont;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:1;text-rendering:optimizeLegibility;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;-moz-osx-font-smoothing:grayscale;font-size:16px;width:16px;height:16px"></i></a></div><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1738272454047-columncontainer-responsivegrid-responsivegr