852493"><div class="rt-content" data-rte-editelement="true">2024 editions</div></h2><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1706819042835-columncontainer_copy-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-title_66608087_copy__1714978590"><h3 class="text-h3-xs lg:text-h3-lg xl:text-h3-xl font-semibold mb-4 lg:mb-5 semantic-text-heading" id="title_1552930796"><div class="rt-content" data-rte-editelement="true">December 2024</div></h3><div></div></div><div class=" aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--8" id="about-us-economic-markets-research-consumer-confidence-jcr-content-root-responsivegrid-tabs_copy_copy-item_1706819042835-columncontainer_copy-responsivegrid-responsivegrid-text_2064119929_copy_840471063"><div class="rt-content" id="_content_anzconz_nz_en_about-us_economic-markets-research_consumer-confidence_jcr_content_root_responsivegrid_tabs_copy_copy_item_1706819042835_columncontainer_copy_responsivegrid_responsivegrid_text_2064119929_copy_840471063" data-rte-editelement="true"><p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence finally cracked triple figures in December, rising marginally from 99.8 to 100.2.</p>
<p>In a welcome sign for retailers, there was another sharp lift in the proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item.</p>
<p>Inflation expectations eased back 0.2%pts to 3.8%, where they’ve spent four of the past five months.</p>
