{"category":"content","componentType":"body-cta"},"iconLeft":{"alt":"","provider":null,"src":null},"iconRight":{"alt":"","provider":null,"src":null},"link":{"dataLayer":{"category":"content"},"href":"/content/dam/anzconz/documents/economics-and-market-research/2025/ANZ-ConsumerConfidence-20250131.pdf","meta":{"extension":"PDF","size":"651.5KB"},"target":"_blank","title":"ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence, January 2025: A softer start to the year","type":"download"}},"standalonecta_166377_727565495":{":type":"anzconz/components/content/standalonecta","button":{"variation":"tertiary"},"dataLayer":{"category":"content","componentType":"body-cta"},"iconLeft":{"alt":"","provider":null,"src":null},"iconRight":{"alt":"","provider":null,"src":null},"link":{"dataLayer":{"category":"content"},"href":"/content/dam/anzconz/documents/economics-and-market-research/2025/ANZ-ConsumerConfidence-20250328.pdf","meta":{"extension":"PDF","size":"756.2KB"},"target":"_blank","title":"ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence, March 2025: Bit of a slog","type":"download"}},"standalonecta_166377_754981211":{":type":"anzconz/components/content/standalonecta","button":{"variation":"tertiary"},"dataLayer":{"category":"content","componentType":"body-cta"},"iconLeft":{"alt":"","provider":null,"src":null},"iconRight":{"alt":"","provider":null,"src":null},"link":{"dataLayer":{"category":"content"},"href":"/content/dam/anzconz/documents/economics-and-market-research/2025/ANZ-ConsumerConfidence-20250424.pdf","meta":{"extension":"PDF","size":"671.7KB"},"target":"_blank","title":"ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence, April 2025: Back on the up","type":"download"}},"standalonecta_166377_760488636":{":type":"anzconz/components/content/standalonecta","button":{"variation":"tertiary"},"dataLayer":{"category":"content","componentType":"body-cta"},"iconLeft":{"alt":"","provider":null,"src":null},"iconRight":{"alt":"","provider":null,"src":null},"link":{"dataLayer":{"category":"content"},"href":"/content/dam/anzconz/documents/economics-and-market-research/2025/ANZ-ConsumerConfidence-20250228.pdf","meta":{"extension":"PDF","size":"756.8KB"},"target":"_blank","title":"ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence, February 2025: Wait-and-see mode","type":"download"}},"standalonecta_1966321415":{":type":"anzconz/components/content/standalonecta","button":{"variation":"tertiary"},"dataLayer":{"category":"content","componentType":"body-cta"},"iconLeft":{"alt":"","provider":null,"src":null},"iconRight":{"alt":"","provider":null,"src":null},"link":{"dataLayer":{"category":"content"},"href":"/content/dam/anzconz/documents/economics-and-market-research/2025/ANZ-ConsumerConfidence-20250627.pdf","meta":{"extension":"PDF","size":"693.3KB"},"target":"_blank","title":"ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence, June 2025: A wintry sunrise","type":"download"}},"text":{":type":"anzconz/components/text","dataLayer":{"componentType":"body-link"},"richText":true,"text":"<p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence fell 5 points to 92.9 in May, giving up the lift seen in April.&nbsp; The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) lifted 1 point, but at -10 it’s still weak. Inflation expectations eased 0.1pts to 4.6%. That’s a lot higher than a couple of months ago, with the jump possibly caused by global tariff talk.&nbsp;</p>\r\n"},"text_1848906934":{":type":"anzconz/components/text","dataLayer":{"componentType":"body-link"},"richText":true,"text":"<p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence fell 4 points to 94.7 in July, continuing its recent zig-zag pattern. The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) fell 1 point to -8, remaining very weak. Inflation expectations lifted 0.2pts to 5.1%, the highest since April 2023. Food price inflation of 4.2% y/y probably has a lot to do with it.&nbsp;</p>\r\n"},"text_1848906934_copy":{":type":"anzconz/components/text","dataLayer":{"componentType":"body-link"},"richText":true,"text":"<p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence fell 3 points to 92 in August, its lowest level in 10 months. The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) fell 4 points to -12. Inflation expectations fell 0.3pts to 4.8%.&nbsp;</p>\r\n"},"text_1848906934_copy_365528341":{":type":"anzconz/components/text","dataLayer":{"componentType":"body-link"},"richText":true,"text":"<p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence rose from 92.0 to 94.6 in September, unwinding the fall seen last month. Confidence was markedly lower in the days following the release of the very weak Q2 GDP data. The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) rose 1 point to -11. Inflation expectations were steady at 4.8%.</p>\r\n"},"text_2064119929_copy":{":type":"anzconz/components/text","dataLayer":{"componentType":"body-link"},"richText":true,"text":"<p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence fell 4 points to 96.0 in January.&nbsp; The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item, the best retail indicator, dropped a sharp 15 points to -16. Inflation expectations were little changed at 3.9%. They have been very stable in recent months.&nbsp;</p>\r\n"},"text_2064119929_copy_2099526448":{":type":"anzconz/components/text","dataLayer":{"componentType":"body-link"},"richText":true,"text":"<p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence rose marginally to 96.6 in February. The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item, the best retail indicator, lifted 1 point to -15. Inflation expectations were little changed at 4.0%, continuing their stable run.</p>\r\n"},"text_2064119929_copy_250696936":{":type":"anzconz/components/text","dataLayer":{"componentType":"body-link"},"richText":true,"text":"<p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence rose 5 points to 98.3 in April, shoring up the upward trend that was starting to look wobbly.&nbsp; The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) rose 5 points, but at -11 it’s still nothing flash. Inflation expectations soared 0.5pts to 4.7%, the highest reading since July 2023. It may be related to global tariff talk, but since New Zealand is not putting on new tariffs, global developments are unlikely to be inflationary here.</p>\r\n"},"text_2064119929_copy_878165270":{":type":"anzconz/components/text","dataLayer":{"componentType":"body-link"},"richText":true,"text":"<p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence fell 4 points to 93.2 in March. While it’s still trending higher, it’s fair to say it’s making hard work of it.&nbsp; The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item, the best retail indicator, eased 1 point to -16.&nbsp;Inflation expectations rose 0.2%pts to 4.2%. While that’s a small increase, it’s the first time since June 2024 that expectations have been above 4%.</p>\r\n"},"text_492601635":{":type":"anzconz/components/text","dataLayer":{"componentType":"body-link"},"richText":true,"text":"<p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence lifted 6 points to 98.8 in June, a welcome bounce after a fall last month.&nbsp;The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) lifted 3 points, but at -7 it’s very soft. Inflation expectations lifted 0.3pts to 4.9%, the highest since April 2023. That’s probably got quite a lot to do with food price inflation, which is running at 4.4%.</p>\r\n"},"text_803677586":{":type":"anzconz/components/text","dataLayer":{"componentType":"body-link"},"richText":true,"text":"<p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence fell slightly from 94.6 to 92.4 in October, giving up last month’s gains.</p>\r\n<p>The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) fell from -11 to -14. This indicator hasn’t been positive in more than four years.</p>\r\n<p>Inflation expectations lifted from 4.8% to 5.1%.</p>\r\n"},"text_803677586_copy":{":type":"anzconz/components/text","dataLayer":{"componentType":"body-link"},"richText":true,"text":"<p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence lifted 6 points from 92.4 to 98.4 in November, the highest level since June.</p>\r\n<p>The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) rose 5 points but is still net negative at -9. This indicator hasn’t been positive in more than four years.</p>\r\n<p>Inflation expectations lifted slightly from 5.1% to 5.2%.</p>\r\n"},"text_803677586_copy_":{":type":"anzconz/components/text","dataLayer":{"componentType":"body-link"},"richText":true,"text":"<p>ANZ-Roy Morgan Consumer Confidence lifted 3 points from 98.4 to 101.5 in December, the highest level since September 2021.</p>\r\n<p>The proportion of households thinking it’s a good time to buy a major household item (the best retail indicator) rose 8 points to -1. This indicator hasn’t been positive in more than four years but is knocking on the door.</p>\r\n<p>Inflation expectations eased from 5.2% to 4.6%, consistent with easing food price inflation.</p>\r\n"},"title":{":type":"anzconz/components/title","anchor":"title_1775033145","contentID":"title_1775033145","title":"May 2025","variation":"H3"},"title_1164321089":{":type":"anzconz/components/title","anchor":"title_611043135","contentID":"title_611043135","title":"July 2025","variation":"H3"},"title_1164321089_cop":{":type":"anzconz/components/title","anchor":"title_294828166","contentID":"title_294828166","title":"August 2025","variation":"H3"},"title_1164321089_cop_1018188616":{":type":"anzconz/components/title","anchor":"title_138561785","contentID":"title_138561785","title":"November 2025","variation":"H3"},"title_1164321089_cop_1077296375":{":type":"anzconz/components/title","anchor":"title_870352344","contentID":"title_870352344","title":"September 2